पाद् पाद् (fr. rt. 2. पद्), see 3. पद्, p. 529;
used at the end of comps., cf. द्वि-पाद्, त्रि-पाद्,
and see

पदि, इस्, m. (according to the Nirukta = गन्तु),
Ved. an animal which uses its feet for locomotion;
a bird; a particular kind of animal (?).

पद्र पद्र, अस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. 2. पद्),
a village; the entrance into a village; the earth;
a particular district.
